Close your eyes and focus on the sound.

30
00:03:09,540 --> 00:03:13,910
Can you hear the bass?
The level is different.

31
00:03:35,070 --> 00:03:38,940
Yeah, yeah. Yeah, I'm about to go there.

32
00:03:38,940 --> 00:03:42,410
Well, don't get pissed.
Okay, I'll be there.

33
00:03:42,410 --> 00:03:44,240
Ryusuke-kun, is something wrong?

34
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:47,150
Yeah, something came up.

35
00:03:47,150 --> 00:03:51,050
He was awfully mad.

36
00:03:51,050 --> 00:03:54,090
Didn't you hear me? I said no thanks.

37
00:03:54,090 --> 00:03:56,850
I told you I'm just waiting for my brother,

38
00:03:56,850 --> 00:03:58,790
not for fuckin' guys like you.

39
00:03:58,790 --> 00:04:01,430
I'm not a whore like you think!

40
00:04:01,430 --> 00:04:03,860
No, I didn't mean it! Sorry.

41
00:04:03,860 --> 00:04:07,000
Bullshit, you fuckin' bastard! Go away!

42
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:10,600
Wow...You're too scary.

43
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:14,440
Scary?! Who do you think makes me scary?

44
00:04:19,110 --> 00:04:21,180
Hey, what's going on? Who are they?

45
00:04:21,180 --> 00:04:25,480
Well, they were hitting on me.
They should go to hell.

46
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:27,550
They're both freaked out like shit.

47
00:04:27,550 --> 00:04:28,850
'Cuz you're late!

48
00:04:28,850 --> 00:04:31,010
Well, sorry about that.

49
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:40,300
Oh, yeah. Let me introduce you.

50
00:04:40,300 --> 00:04:43,270
Koyuki is 14, same as you, Maho.

51
00:04:43,270 --> 00:04:44,400
I know!

52
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:47,770
-And what'll you have?
-Whatever.

53
00:04:47,770 --> 00:04:51,380
Okay, then. Koyuki, take care of it.

54
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:53,610
I'm going to talk to Taira, the bassist.

55
00:04:53,610 --> 00:04:57,980
I've gotta catch him early,
or he'll be taken.

56
00:04:57,980 --> 00:05:02,890
The main thing in a band is...
a bassist and drummer.

57
00:05:02,890 --> 00:05:04,720
Is a beef bowl okay?

58
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:15,830
Okay, see you later.

59
00:05:15,830 --> 00:05:18,670
I called some friends from school.
You don't mind, do you?

60
00:05:18,670 --> 00:05:20,330
Sure.

61
00:05:23,140 --> 00:05:27,780
Say, the other day, I met this guy,
and he tried to pick me up!

62
00:05:27,780 --> 00:05:30,050
But he was such an asshole!

63
00:05:30,050 --> 00:05:32,380
But he had a BMW convertible!

64
00:05:32,380 --> 00:05:35,890
Really? That's cool! I love that car!

65
00:05:35,890 --> 00:05:38,690
I know...But he was awfully creepy!

66
00:05:38,690 --> 00:05:42,150
His eyes twitched in this weird way
and it made me sick!

67
00:05:44,630 --> 00:05:47,060
But Risa, you always
get stuck with weirdos.

68
00:05:47,060 --> 00:05:48,070
I know...

69
00:05:48,070 --> 00:05:51,140
Why don't you wait for Maho's rejects?

70
00:05:51,140 --> 00:05:53,170
Oh no. Some poor-looking foreigners
hit on me earlier.

71
00:05:53,170 --> 00:05:56,640
-Poor foreigners? That sucks!
-Yeah...

72
00:05:56,640 --> 00:06:00,270
There's never cool guys.
I like guys riding Porsches.

73
00:06:01,710 --> 00:06:04,150
-Then I want a Ferrari.
-Me too!

74
00:06:05,350 --> 00:06:08,250
Hey, let's go clubbing now.
We might find our dream guy.

75
00:06:08,250 --> 00:06:10,290
Yay, let's go!

76
00:06:10,290 --> 00:06:12,990
Yeah, I wanna go, but I'm broke.

77
00:06:12,990 --> 00:06:14,530
-Umm...I...
-Come on!

78
00:06:14,530 --> 00:06:16,530
Fine, the dream guy will pay for you.

79
00:06:16,530 --> 00:06:19,300
Yeah, free buy!

80
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:22,960
I have something to
take care of, so I'll be going.

81
00:06:28,670 --> 00:06:32,630
They don't teach English properly
in Japan, is what I feel.

82
00:06:33,880 --> 00:06:35,750
Dutch, huh?

83
00:06:35,750 --> 00:06:38,320
Your Japanese has improved.

84
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:40,380
Is that meant to be a compliment?

85
00:06:42,050 --> 00:06:45,020
Eiji and I jammed the other day.

86
00:06:46,760 --> 00:06:49,620
He's getting better, amazingly fast.

87
00:06:52,030 --> 00:06:57,130
I finish school this year,
and I'm thinking seriously about my future.

88
00:06:57,130 --> 00:07:00,230
If you want to make music with me,
bring me a really great vocalist.

89
00:07:15,420 --> 00:07:17,220
A vocalist, huh?

90
00:07:33,100 --> 00:07:34,440
Yo!

91
00:07:37,240 --> 00:07:38,880
W-what happened?

92
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:42,870
I have no place to crash tonight.
So I'm going to Ryusuke's place.

93
00:07:44,980 --> 00:07:46,810
Umm, the other day...

94
00:07:48,650 --> 00:07:52,060
I'm sorry I laughed at you
about not knowing kanji.

95
00:07:52,060 --> 00:07:56,530
Don't worry about it.
Besides, I am bad at kanji.

96
00:07:56,530 --> 00:07:59,930
I got fired from a diner yesterday
because I didn't know the language.

97
00:07:59,930 --> 00:08:00,700
Are you serious?

98
00:08:00,700 --> 00:08:05,360
I was so mad, I yelled and cried
that I was going back to America.

99
00:08:09,140 --> 00:08:11,040
Then my dad slapped me.

100
00:08:12,310 --> 00:08:13,870
Are you all right?

101
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:20,180
You're very kind, Koyuki.

102
00:08:22,090 --> 00:08:25,360
But you don't seem to like my friends.

103
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:28,460
B-because I left early?

104
00:08:28,460 --> 00:08:31,460
You didn't try to talk to them.

105
00:08:31,460 --> 00:08:35,830
-But the language...
-ls that it? The language?

106
00:08:35,830 --> 00:08:38,200
Everyone says the same thing.

107
00:08:38,200 --> 00:08:39,970
Well, let's go see Beck!

108
00:08:39,970 --> 00:08:42,440
Huh? Beck?!

109
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:46,240
Beck!

110
00:08:58,660 --> 00:09:02,330
Hey, Beck! I haven't seen you
in a while, yet you ignore me!

111
00:09:02,330 --> 00:09:04,630
Please help me, Maho-chan!

112
00:09:04,630 --> 00:09:06,720
Stop adding "-chan" to my name.

113
00:09:10,130 --> 00:09:12,170
Hi, Beck...

114
00:09:12,170 --> 00:09:13,800
How's it going?

115
00:09:15,510 --> 00:09:18,000
Brother taking care of you?

116
00:09:20,310 --> 00:09:22,540
Such a pretty full moon.

117
00:09:25,920 --> 00:09:28,090
It's a full moon tonight.

118
00:09:28,090 --> 00:09:33,680
Full moon sways...

119
00:09:35,190 --> 00:09:40,650
Gently in the night of one fine day...

120
00:09:43,030 --> 00:09:47,770
Maho, you're amazing. You can
speak English and you sing great.

121
00:09:47,770 --> 00:09:49,240
And you're cute...

122
00:09:49,240 --> 00:09:51,140
I know you'll make it as a singer!

123
00:09:51,140 --> 00:09:52,380
As if!

124
00:09:52,380 --> 00:09:56,050
I have no talent as a singer.

125
00:09:56,050 --> 00:09:59,950
My dream is to study movies in New York.

126
00:10:11,130 --> 00:10:18,800
Full moon sways...

127
00:10:18,800 --> 00:10:25,470
Gently in the night of one fine day.

128
00:10:26,980 --> 00:10:33,440
On my way...

129
00:10:34,790 --> 00:10:41,710
Looking for a moment with my dear...

130
00:10:49,470 --> 00:10:52,660
It's my favorite song by Dying Breed.

131
00:11:11,920 --> 00:11:13,720
Hey, Tanaka!

132
00:11:19,030 --> 00:11:20,630
Find something?

133
00:11:20,630 --> 00:11:24,860
Oh, it's you, Izumi-chan!
Don't scare me like that!

134
00:11:26,200 --> 00:11:29,270
-So, are you willing?
-Huh?

135
00:11:29,270 --> 00:11:33,180
Stop by the municipal pool at 6 pm.

136
00:11:33,180 --> 00:11:35,180
Pool?

137
00:11:35,180 --> 00:11:38,910
Don't be late, now.
You'll find out when you get there.

138
00:11:40,420 --> 00:11:42,180
The municipal pool?

139
00:11:46,490 --> 00:11:48,290
Well then, I'll see you later.

140
00:11:48,290 --> 00:11:49,090
"Business envelopes, fabric tape,
