5:30 huh?

149
00:12:05,940 --> 00:12:07,670
There!

150
00:12:09,410 --> 00:12:11,380
And now...

151
00:12:20,060 --> 00:12:22,830
Hey, kid...

152
00:12:22,830 --> 00:12:26,130
Please don't grab onto the lane ropes.

153
00:12:26,130 --> 00:12:29,170
I know, but...

154
00:12:29,170 --> 00:12:35,470
Hey, kid! If you're in the
50 meter pool, don't stop!

155
00:12:49,020 --> 00:12:53,160
-There he is.
-Let's go home.

156
00:12:53,160 --> 00:12:55,790
Hey, your kick is okay,

157
00:12:55,790 --> 00:13:00,130
but you pull with your elbow,
so you're not cutting into the water.

158
00:13:00,130 --> 00:13:02,170
Huh? Oh...

159
00:13:02,170 --> 00:13:05,620
Okay! Hook your feet
against the pool and practice!

160
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:10,870
-Let's give it a try!
-W-who is he?

161
00:13:10,870 --> 00:13:13,810
He's the famous man of this pool.

162
00:13:13,810 --> 00:13:15,180
Famous?

163
00:13:15,180 --> 00:13:19,380
His name's Saito-san, and he
was once an Olympic swimmer.

164
00:13:19,380 --> 00:13:23,690
So whenever he sees a poor swimmer,
he can't help but teach.

165
00:13:23,690 --> 00:13:25,290
An Olympic swimmer?

166
00:13:25,290 --> 00:13:28,220
Well, he's not a bad guy.

167
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:34,500
Huh? That's strange...

168
00:13:34,500 --> 00:13:36,470
Izumi!

169
00:13:36,470 --> 00:13:39,400
He's in the 25-meter pool.

170
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:44,510
One, two, three, four...

171
00:13:44,510 --> 00:13:47,080
Just as I figured!

172
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:50,150
Koyuki got caught!

173
00:13:50,150 --> 00:13:53,580
Kid, are you ready?

174
00:13:53,580 --> 00:13:55,690
You're giving me a
15-meter handicap, right?

175
00:13:55,690 --> 00:14:00,290
Yeah...This is serious, a real contest.

176
00:14:00,290 --> 00:14:02,930
Yes. And if I win?

177
00:14:02,930 --> 00:14:07,000
As promised, I'll train you man to man.

178
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:07,700
All right.

179
00:14:07,700 --> 00:14:10,700
-And if you lose...
-lf I lose?

180
00:14:10,700 --> 00:14:12,170
I'll hit you!

181
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:17,840
Huh?!

182
00:14:17,840 --> 00:14:20,610
And I won't hold back!

183
00:14:20,610 --> 00:14:21,880
Why would you do that?!

184
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:27,050
Kid...In the grown-up world,
there are many painful things!

185
00:14:27,050 --> 00:14:29,550
Now get set!

186
00:14:29,550 --> 00:14:31,280
Ready!

187
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:33,960
Go!

188
00:14:38,330 --> 00:14:39,920
Five meters.

189
00:14:41,630 --> 00:14:43,220
Ten meters.

190
00:14:44,900 --> 00:14:48,770
Fifteen meters!

191
00:14:58,750 --> 00:15:01,310
Victory is mine!

192
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:15,630
I...did it!

193
00:15:17,470 --> 00:15:18,870
Saito-san...

194
00:15:20,540 --> 00:15:22,070
It's been a long time.

195
00:15:22,070 --> 00:15:23,600
Izumi-chan!

196
00:15:27,010 --> 00:15:27,780
Oh!

197
00:15:27,780 --> 00:15:32,220
You're in the swim club at my alma mater,
Ihara East Middle School!

198
00:15:32,220 --> 00:15:34,820
How is Suzuki-sensei's lumbago?

199
00:15:34,820 --> 00:15:37,290
I think it's much better.

200
00:15:37,290 --> 00:15:39,790
Saito-san, please come
and coach us again!

201
00:15:39,790 --> 00:15:43,590
Oh, really? I'm glad that
someone like you appreciates me!

202
00:15:46,760 --> 00:15:49,970
-Then you talked to him?
-Yeah.

203
00:15:49,970 --> 00:15:51,460
You're really...

204
00:15:52,600 --> 00:15:56,740
I asked him for some advice. And then...

205
00:15:56,740 --> 00:15:58,840
And then?

206
00:15:58,840 --> 00:16:03,180
We somehow wound up in a race.

207
00:16:03,180 --> 00:16:04,410
Koyuki-kun!

208
00:16:06,420 --> 00:16:07,850
Want some?

209
00:16:07,850 --> 00:16:10,420
-N-no, thank you.
-No?

210
00:16:10,420 --> 00:16:14,690
Well, let's practice again tomorrow!
Good night!

211
00:16:18,430 --> 00:16:20,360
He's like a different person.

212
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:25,330
Saito-san is a really warm-hearted
gentleman outside the pool.

213
00:16:27,540 --> 00:16:31,810
He listens to U.K. Rock bands, I think.

214
00:16:31,810 --> 00:16:33,180
U.K.?

215
00:16:33,180 --> 00:16:37,850
English rock bands.
Like the Beatles and stuff.

216
00:16:37,850 --> 00:16:40,050
The Stones are British, too, right?

217
00:16:40,050 --> 00:16:43,450
Yes, the Zeppelin too.

218
00:16:43,450 --> 00:16:45,390
I feel like I'm in the way.

219
00:16:45,390 --> 00:16:47,020
Huh?

220
00:16:47,020 --> 00:16:50,460
I have an early curfew. Good night!

221
00:16:53,460 --> 00:16:57,400
-Is swimming fun?
-Yeah.

222
00:16:57,400 --> 00:17:00,500
-Think you'll continue?
-Yeah.

223
00:17:00,500 --> 00:17:02,560
Really? I'm glad.

224
00:17:04,510 --> 00:17:08,650
I was going to stop by
Ryusuke-kun's place.

225
00:17:08,650 --> 00:17:10,770
Maybe I'll join you.

226
00:17:17,690 --> 00:17:19,660
You have a game on Sunday?

227
00:17:19,660 --> 00:17:21,730
Yeah, Mit-chan asked me.

228
00:17:21,730 --> 00:17:23,630
Umm...your grip...

229
00:17:25,230 --> 00:17:29,600
-He just needed a player...
-Ryusuke-kun, your grip...

230
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:31,970
Huh? You say something, Koyuki?

231
00:17:31,970 --> 00:17:36,070
Koyuki has a present for you, Ryusuke-kun.

232
00:17:36,070 --> 00:17:37,540
A present?

233
00:17:39,510 --> 00:17:42,480
An unleashed dog may be taken away.

234
00:17:42,480 --> 00:17:47,250
I have been worried
how he doesn't come home lately...

235
00:17:50,150 --> 00:17:51,480
Wait a minute.

236
00:17:55,490 --> 00:17:57,320
Damn, it's dusty.

237
00:17:59,760 --> 00:18:02,730
You can have this.

238
00:18:02,730 --> 00:18:03,530
No way!

239
00:18:03,530 --> 00:18:06,600
You've been listening
to a lot of music lately.

240
00:18:06,600 --> 00:18:09,660
I figured you might want to play, too.

241
00:18:10,770 --> 00:18:13,140
It looks quite old.

242
00:18:17,410 --> 00:18:20,650
It's not much, but the sound is good.

243
00:18:20,650 --> 00:18:22,520
Wow!

244
00:18:22,520 --> 00:18:24,210
There we go.

245
00:18:57,620 --> 00:19:01,160
-A string broke.
-What song was that?

246
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:03,930
-I just played whatever.
-It's the blues, right?

247
00:19:03,930 --> 00:19:05,200
Yeah.

248
00:19:05,200 --> 00:19:08,100
I love the way you play, Ryusuke-kun.

249
00:19:11,640 --> 00:19:17,070
I'm gonna play every waking moment
and get better and better!

250
00:19:17,070 --> 00:19:19,170
Huh? Yeah.

251
00:19:23,080 --> 00:19:27,450
Oh, Ryusuke-kun!
Mit-chan is steaming mad!

252
00:19:27,450 --> 00:19:30,950
-Wasn't it at 4:30?
-No, 3:00!

253
00:19:30,950 --> 00:19:32,620
It's already the last inning!

254
00:19:32,620 --> 00:19:34,020
I heard 4:30.

255
00:19:37,990 --> 00:19:39,900
Who's that pitcher?

256
00:19:39,900 --> 00:19:43,270
The vocalist for The Crowd,
Manabu Miyazawa.

257
00:19:43,270 --> 00:19:44,700
Is he famous?

258
00:19:44,700 --> 00:19:46,600
The Crowd had a huge following

259
00:19:46,600 --> 00:19:49,810
and people thought it was
a matter of time before they debuted.

260
00:19:49,810 --> 00:19:53,280
But the drummer suddenly quit
and the band broke up.

261
00:19:53,280 --> 00:19:56,010
The end was really pitiful.

262
00:20:00,880 --> 00:20:03,390
-Hey! Where're you throwing?!
-Oops! That's weird!

263
00:20:03,390 --> 00:20:05,350
I can't hit the bat!

264
00:20:06,360 --> 00:20:09,120
Batter! Don't move too much!

265
00:20:14,830 --> 00:20:17,630
-Strike!
-He doesn't seem so great...

266
00:20:17,630 --> 00:20:22,610
If he joins my band,
Taira-kun will join, too.

267
00:20:22,610 --> 00:20:26,810
Ryusuke-kun...Look at the other bench.

268
00:20:26,810 --> 00:20:28,750
Eiji...

269
00:20:28,750 --> 00:20:33,750
He's been asking Manabu-kun
to join since the Serial Mama stuff.

270
00:20:33,750 --> 00:20:35,290
Hey, Ryusuke!

271
00:20:35,290 --> 00:20:39,020
-Do you know what time it is?!
-Sorry, I had the wrong time.

272
00:20:39,020 --> 00:20:41,730
I told you we had just enough players.

273
00:20:41,730 --> 00:20:42,530
Sorry.

274
00:20:42,530 --> 00:20:47,830
'Cuz of you, I had to call the
one person in the world I didn't wanna.

275
00:20:47,830 --> 00:20:50,960
Not...Chiba?

276
00:20:53,900 --> 00:20:55,740
Ryusuke-kun?

277
00:20:55,740 --> 00:21:01,280
-I owe him 30,000 yen.
-Hey! Where's my money?!

278
00:21:01,280 --> 00:21:04,110
"Pay when you can."
Don't they have that in Japan?

279
00:21:04,110 --> 00:21:06,950
Shut up! You ingrate!

280
00:21:06,950 --> 00:21:12,460
Chiba! We only have the field
'til 5:00! Hurry it up!

281
00:21:12,460 --> 00:21:15,260
Just you wait, Ryusuke.

282
00:21:15,260 --> 00:21:16,380
Awright!

283
00:21:18,660 --> 00:21:19,820
Ball!

284
00:21:21,400 --> 00:21:24,730
Frankly, I don't care for Manabu's vocals.

285
00:21:24,730 --> 00:21:28,070
But in order to get Taira-kun,
I have no choice.

286
00:21:28,070 --> 00:21:32,980
-Then what about Chiba?
-Huh? I've never heard him sing.

287
00:21:32,980 --> 00:21:37,080
Chiba has charisma. He has
more aura than Manabu-kun.

288
00:21:37,080 --> 00:21:38,880
Oww!

289
00:21:39,820 --> 00:21:42,550
You should've moved!

290
00:21:44,020 --> 00:21:46,520
Dammit! I'll kill you!

291
00:21:46,520 --> 00:21:49,590
Oh, c'mon, don't get so uptight.

292
00:21:49,590 --> 00:21:52,100
You're the losers anyway.

293
00:21:52,100 --> 00:21:53,430
Calm down.

294
00:21:55,670 --> 00:21:58,430
Don't touch me!

295
00:22:00,100 --> 00:22:02,400
Oh well...

296
00:22:11,780 --> 00:22:13,310
Stop...

297
00:22:20,820 --> 00:22:28,320
Stop!

298
00:22:35,210 --> 00:22:37,070
Koyuki...

299
00:22:50,380 --> 00:22:52,480
Another minute

300
00:22:52,480 --> 00:22:55,350
Feelin' so fine

301
00:22:57,480 --> 00:22:59,720
You turn the freeze

302
00:22:59,720 --> 00:23:02,450
into warm light

303
00:23:04,560 --> 00:23:08,130
Had a premonition

304
00:23:08,130 --> 00:23:10,830
I've been waitin' ever since

305
00:23:10,830 --> 00:23:14,330
My world comin' down

306
00:23:14,330 --> 00:23:16,930
It's got me spinnin' 'round

307
00:23:18,910 --> 00:23:25,250
If you really wanna fly

308
00:23:25,250 --> 00:23:27,980
you gotta let go

309
00:23:40,090 --> 00:23:42,430
Simply the most

310
00:23:42,430 --> 00:23:44,460
big sensation

311
00:23:44,460 --> 00:23:47,270
(once you're here you won't go back)

312
00:23:47,270 --> 00:23:49,540
She's really pretty

313
00:23:49,540 --> 00:23:51,870
One-eyed vision

314
00:23:51,870 --> 00:23:54,370
(lose the fear it don't come back)

315
00:23:54,370 --> 00:23:58,040
Little sister showed me

316
00:23:58,040 --> 00:24:00,680
Really took me for a ride

317
00:24:00,680 --> 00:24:02,280
My world comin' down

318
00:24:02,280 --> 00:24:05,750
(once you're here you won't go back)

319
00:24:05,750 --> 00:24:09,710
(lose the fear it don't come back)

320
00:24:13,990 --> 00:24:16,300
I like Kasumi-chan of the tobacco shop.

321
00:24:16,300 --> 00:24:16,830
"Next Episode"

322
00:24:16,300 --> 00:24:16,830
I like Kasumi-chan of the tobacco shop.

323
00:24:16,830 --> 00:24:19,930
"Next Episode"

324
00:24:16,830 --> 00:24:19,930
But I also like Ranko-chan
of the family restaurant.

325
